{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_04_agent_protocol_s3_1", "label": "04 \u00a73.1 \u2014 Blind independent verification and no self-certification", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-34-first-pass-self-check.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_10_agent_handoff_invariant_7", "label": "Invariant 7 \u2014 AI is never evidence by itself (MODEL_OUTPUT weighs 0)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-34-first-pass-self-check.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "implementation_implemented_stage_34_first_pass_self_check_stage", "label": "Stage 34 \u2014 A person can finish their own investigation (implemented)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-34-first-pass-self-check.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A person outlined a two-hour source into 247 claims over 1,679 signed writes, and all 742 verification tasks behind them were closed to them, so the outline read \"182 unresolved\" until a stranger arrived. That is a dead end for the only user the node has, and a bad trade: it protected a number nobody is reading yet at the cost of the product being finishable."}, {"id": "implementation_implemented_stage_34_first_pass_self_check_code_stricter_than_spec", "label": "The code was stricter than the spec, so no amendment was needed", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-34-first-pass-self-check.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "04 \u00a73.1 forbids exactly two things \u2014 auditing your own contribution and accepting your own proposed claim \u2014 and neither is a task type. Tasks::Lease applied its self-authorship guard to every type, so EVIDENCE_VERIFICATION, OPPOSING_EVIDENCE_SEARCH and QUALIFIER_CHECK were blocked along with audits. That extra strictness, not the rule, is what made a solo investigation unfinishable."}, {"id": "implementation_implemented_stage_34_first_pass_self_check_no_accuracy_rating", "label": "No free-standing accuracy rating; the task outcomes are the rating", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-34-first-pass-self-check.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The owner asked for \"their own accuracy score\", and the instinct is right, but a new rating would be the assistant's own judgement with a number attached \u2014 MODEL_OUTPUT, which Invariant 7 weighs at zero. The verification task outcomes are already a closed, server-validated enum with the reading behind them, so unlocking them gives what was asked and invents nothing."}, {"id": "implementation_implemented_stage_34_first_pass_self_check_filtered_before_scorer", "label": "Self-checks are filtered before the scorer, not flagged inside it", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-34-first-pass-self-check.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Tasks::Checks.for excludes self-performed results so they never enter task_checks and cannot move review_coverage \u2014 the whole safety of the stage. A flag would change the shape of the scoring trace, and Invariant 4 then requires a new model version, new config, new goldens and a reference-scorer pass for a feature that must not move the number anyway. Excluding keeps every existing trace byte-identical."}, {"id": "implementation_implemented_stage_34_first_pass_self_check_self_performed_column", "label": "self_performed recorded at lease time, never recomputed", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-34-first-pass-self-check.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deriving it later by comparing principals would change as keys are adopted and contributors merge; a fact about what happened must not be recomputed from a world that has since changed."}, {"id": "implementation_implemented_stage_34_first_pass_self_check_share_line_three_numbers", "label": "The share line names all three numbers", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-34-first-pass-self-check.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "\"247 claims \u00b7 247 self-checked \u00b7 0 independently checked\" rather than the shorter \"none independently checked\": it is what someone pasting the link is publishing about their own work, it states the weakness in the same breath as the volume, and it keeps reading correctly as the second number falls behind the third."}, {"id": "implementation_implemented_stage_34_first_pass_self_check_blind_requested", "label": "blind_requested \u2014 splitting a deliberate blind hand-off from routine opening", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-34-first-pass-self-check.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Stage 19's guard \"whoever asks for a blind check does not perform it\" keyed on created_by, which is set both when someone deliberately calls open_task and when verification opens routinely alongside a recording. created_by cannot tell them apart, so tasks now carry blind_requested, true only for the deliberate case; without it, narrowing the first guard would have achieved nothing."}, {"id": "implementation_implemented_stage_34_first_pass_self_check_instructions_drift", "label": "Instructions describing behaviour the code no longer has", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-34-first-pass-self-check.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The next_task description and Guidance::OUTLINE still said a principal never gets a check on its own claim, and the full suite passed against instructions that contradicted the code they described \u2014 the third time the project shipped a behaviour change while the thing an assistant reads kept describing the old one."}], "edges": [{"source": "implementation_implemented_stage_34_first_pass_self_check_stage", "target": "implementation_implemented_stage_34_first_pass_self_check_code_stricter_than_spec", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-34-first-pass-self-check.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_implemented_stage_34_first_pass_self_check_stage", "target": "implementation_implemented_stage_34_first_pass_self_check_no_accuracy_rating", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-34-first-pass-self-check.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_implemented_stage_34_first_pass_self_check_stage", "target": "implementation_implemented_stage_34_first_pass_self_check_filtered_before_scorer", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-34-first-pass-self-check.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_implemented_stage_34_first_pass_self_check_stage", "target": "implementation_implemented_stage_34_first_pass_self_check_self_performed_column", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED",